/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Convert the decimal number 218.625 into: \(1\) Binary, \(2\) Octal, and) Tj
T*
(\(3\) Hexadecimal.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Integer Part Conversion \(218\):) Tj
T*
(- 218 / 2 = 109 rem 0 | 109 / 2 = 54 rem 1 | 54 / 2 = 27 rem 0 | 27 / 2 = 13 rem 1 | 13) Tj
T*
(/ 2 = 6 rem 1 | 6 / 2 = 3 rem 0 | 3 / 2 = 1 rem 1 | 1 / 2 = 0 rem 1.) Tj
T*
(- Reading remainders from bottom to top: 218_10 = 11011010_2.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Fractional Part Conversion \(0.625\):) Tj
T*
(- 0.625 x 2 = 1.250 -> Integer 1, fractional 0.250.) Tj
T*
(- 0.250 x 2 = 0.500 -> Integer 0, fractional 0.500.) Tj
T*
(- 0.500 x 2 = 1.000 -> Integer 1, fractional 0.000 \(terminates\).) Tj
T*
(- Reading integers top to bottom: 0.625_10 = 0.101_2.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Binary Result: 218.625_10 = 11011010.101_2.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Conversion to Octal \(Group in 3s from binary point\):) Tj
T*
(- Integer: \(011\) \(011\) \(010\) = 3 3 2.) Tj
T*
(- Fractional: \(101\) = 5.) Tj
T*
(- Octal Result: 332.5_8.) Tj
T*
(* 5. Conversion to Hexadecimal \(Group in 4s from binary point\):) Tj
T*
(- Integer: \(1101\) \(1010\) = D A.) Tj
T*
(- Fractional: \(1010\) = A.) Tj
T*
(- Hexadecimal Result: DA.A_16 or 0xDA.A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
