/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Encode the decimal number -43.75 into 32-bit IEEE 754) Tj
T*
(Single-Precision floating-point format. Express the final bit sequence in Hexadecimal.) Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Derivation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Determine Sign Bit \(S\): Number is negative -> S = 1.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Convert Absolute Value to Binary: 43.75:) Tj
T*
(- 43 = 32 + 8 + 2 + 1 = 101011_2. 0.75 = 0.5 + 0.25 = 0.11_2.) Tj
T*
(- 43.75_10 = 101011.11_2.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Normalize into Scientific Notation \(1.M x 2^e\):) Tj
T*
(- 101011.11 = 1.0101111 x 2^5 \(Shifted binary point 5 positions to the left\). Actual) Tj
T*
(exponent e = 5.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Calculate Biased Exponent \(E\):) Tj
T*
(- E = e + Bias = 5 + 127 = 132.) Tj
T*
(- 132 in 8-bit binary = 128 + 4 = 10000100_2.) Tj
T*
(* 5. Determine 23-bit Mantissa \(M\):) Tj
T*
(- Drop leading 1: M = 01011110000000000000000 \(padded with trailing zeros to 23 bits\).) Tj
T*
(* 6. Assemble 32-bit Pattern:) Tj
T*
(- S \(1 bit\): 1) Tj
T*
(- E \(8 bits\): 10000100) Tj
T*
(- M \(23 bits\): 01011110000000000000000) Tj
T*
(- Concatenated: 1 10000100 01011110000000000000000) Tj
T*
(* 7. Hexadecimal Representation \(Group into nibbles\):) Tj
T*
(- 1100 0010 0010 1111 0000 0000 0000 0000 -> 0xC22F0000.) Tj
T*
