T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: Minimize the Boolean switching function F\(A, B, C, D\) = Sum m\(0, 2,) Tj
T*
(5, 7, 8, 10, 13, 15\) using a 4-variable Karnaugh Map, and draw the equivalent circuit) Tj
T*
(using only universal 2-input NAND gates.) Tj
T*
(K-Map Minimization Protocol:) Tj
T*
(* 1. K-Map Cell Population \(Gray Code grid AB x CD\):) Tj
T*
(- Min-terms at \(0, 2\), \(8, 10\) form a 4-corner quad: m0 \(0000\), m2 \(0010\), m8 \(1000\),) Tj
T*
(m10 \(1010\).) Tj
T*
(- Common variables across the 4 corners: B is 0 \(B''\), D is 0 \(D''\). Term 1 = B''.D''.) Tj
T*
(- Min-terms at \(5, 7, 13, 15\) form an interior quad: m5 \(0101\), m7 \(0111\), m13 \(1101\),) Tj
T*
(m15 \(1111\).) Tj
T*
(- Common variables across the interior quad: B is 1 \(B\), D is 1 \(D\). Term 2 = B.D.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Minimized Sum of Products \(SOP\): F = B''.D'' + B.D \(Notice this is the Boolean) Tj
T*
(equivalence XNOR: F = ~\(B \(+\) D\)\).) Tj
T*
(* 3. Universal NAND Gate Realization:) Tj
T*
(- Apply double negation: F = ~~F = ~\( ~\(B''.D''\) . ~\(B.D\) \).) Tj
T*
(- Invert B and D using NAND gates with tied inputs to produce B'' and D''.) Tj
T*
(- Feed B'' and D'' into NAND gate 1 to produce ~\(B''.D''\).) Tj
T*
(- Feed B and D into NAND gate 2 to produce ~\(B.D\).) Tj
T*
(- Feed the outputs of NAND 1 and NAND 2 into output NAND gate 3 to yield F.) Tj
T*
